# ~/.gitignore_global — OS junk ignored in every repository.
#
# The three ignore tiers, scoped by WHO causes a file to exist:
#   project .gitignore  — what the project produces (build output, env files);
#                         lives in the repo so it protects every contributor
#   this file           — what YOUR operating system produces;
#                         other people's environments are their own job
#   .git/info/exclude   — personal one-offs in a single repo, never committed
#
# Editor files are deliberately NOT listed: no list can know every editor a
# person may use, and editor files are not reliably junk (some teams track
# .idea/ or .vscode/ on purpose) — that policy belongs to each project.
# The one exception is vim (below): it exists on every machine.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments — a # only counts at line start.

# macOS
# Finder folder-view metadata
.DS_Store
# resource forks on non-Apple filesystems
.AppleDouble
# custom "open with" app bindings
.LSOverride
# custom folder icons
Icon?
# AppleDouble sidecar files on external drives
._*
# Spotlight index on external drives
.Spotlight-V100
# trash folder on external drives
.Trashes

# Linux
# KDE folder-view metadata
.directory
# trash folder on external drives
.Trash-*

# Windows
# Explorer thumbnail cache
Thumbs.db
# Explorer folder settings
Desktop.ini

# Vim — exception to the no-editor rule: vim/vi ships with every OS and is
# this setup's fallback editor on headless machines, so its transient swap
# files are environment junk everywhere (and never legitimately tracked).
*.swp
*.swo
